\f1\b\fs36 1. Scene engine\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The elliptical-rail apparatus has been commissioned sufficiently for a full operational test using the original two Gyges discs.\
This is the first scene in which the machine described in 
\f1\b \strokec2 Johnny reveals the first operational elliptical-rail apparatus 
\f2\b0 \strokec2 actually moves through its designed operating envelope.\
The test begins conservatively and becomes progressively more complex. The apparatus changes the discs\'92 relative geometry while maintaining useful interaction between them.\
Nothing catastrophic happens.\
That is the result that matters.\
The machine works substantially as Quark\'92s engineers intended. Previous apparatuses relied heavily on brute rotational speed and tended to lose stability as interacting discs affected one another. The elliptical-rail apparatus can instead manipulate geometry continuously and compensate as the relationship between the discs changes.\
For most of those present, this is success.\
Chip has reasons to find controlled success more troubling than ordinary instability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

