\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 5. What the engineers are actually demonstrating\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Not maximum RPM.\
Not raw mechanical violence.\
The important capability is that the apparatus can 
\f1\b \strokec2 change the relative geometry of two active Gyges discs without immediately losing control of their interaction
\f2\b0 \strokec2 .\
Quark\'92s team can compensate as conditions change.\
The exact control variables need not be enumerated unless required by dialogue or a problem during the test.\
\'93Phase\'94, \'93coherence\'94, \'93geometry\'94, \'93drift\'94, \'93compensation\'94 and similar terms are enough.\
Do not introduce distinctions among multiple kinds of phase unless the scene actually needs them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

